 "rendered_as": "transformers renders a chat template: trim_blocks, lstrip_blocks, loopcontrols, tojson = json.dumps(ensure_ascii=False) with the template's separators",
 "script": "scripts/render_kimi_k2_turns.py",
 "notes": [
  "A turn is the history rendered with the turn's message minus the generation prompt, minus the <|im_end|> that ends it, which the stop decoder hides from the parser.",
  "K2 Instruct and Instruct-0905 write no thought. K2 Thinking's prompt ends at the turn opener and the model writes its own <think>. K2.5's and K2.6's prompt ends with <think>, or with <think></think> when thinking is false; K2.7-Code's with <think>, with no switch. The tail carries the prompt's ending, so the replay starts where the template leaves the model.",
  "The templates that render <think></think> for an answer in the history (K2 Thinking, K2.5, K2.6 without preserve_thinking) keep a thought on a message that calls alone; the thought-and-answer shape is rendered where the template keeps it (K2.7-Code, K2.6 with preserve_thinking).",
  "A call's id is the line's own, functions.NAME:N; the name is read from it. The arguments are given to the template as an object and written with tojson.",
  "A turn two templates render alike is written once, with every template that renders it under rendered_by; the tail is the prompt from its last user or tool message."
 ],
